<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Court of the One Hundred and Four</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Court of the One Hundred and Four was a judicial body of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>. It held generals accountable for military failures, sometimes punishing defeated commanders severely. Its precise composition and powers remain debated among historians of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>.</p></div>
